    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Terrestrial biogeochemical feedbacks",
    "problem": "Climate change projections are challenged by their narrow focus on carbon-cycle interactions, largely ignoring other key terrestrial biogeochemical feedbacks (e.g., nitrogen, ozone) whose combined positive forcing could substantially reduce or even eliminate the cooling effect of CO\u2082 fertilization.",
    "method": "This paper synthesizes and quantifies numerous terrestrial biogeochemical feedbacks by applying a unifying radiative forcing framework to provide a first estimate of their combined magnitude, highlighting their substantial but uncertain impact on the climate system.",
    "task": "The task is to review, link, and provide a first estimate of the magnitude of multiple terrestrial biogeochemical feedbacks, in terms of radiative forcing, to assess their collective impact on the climate system and compare it to that of physical climate feedbacks.",
