            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Figure 2 | Superposed epoch analysis of ice-core and biomass-burning records over the interval 80 ka to 10 ka. This analysis shows the consistent response of a time series to the repeated occurrence of the abrupt warming and cooling events that define the Dansgaard-Oeschger cycles during the last glacial period. Shading indicates significant patterns in the response of the time series to the events of abrupt warming and rapid cooling. a, The Greenland oxygen-isotope record, an index of regional temperature, shows the characteristic saw-tooth pattern of an individual Dansgaard-Oeschger cycle. b\u2013f, Distinctive responses associated with the occurrence of abrupt warming or cooling. BYRD: Byrd station, Antarctica; EDC: EPICA Dome C; NGRIP: North Greenland Ice Core Project. For data sources and further discussion see Supplementary Information.",
